# Jarian Architecture Law #004 — Unified List Infrastructure

**Full doc:** `Docs/architecture/UNIFIED_LIST_INFRASTRUCTURE.md`

All ERP lists MUST use the shared list infrastructure. Per-module sort, filter, resize, status, column manager, or infinite-loading implementations are forbidden.

---

## Mandatory shared capabilities

| Capability | Use |
|---|---|
| Resizable columns | `ResizableTh` + widths via `useListShell` |
| Excel-style filters | `ColumnFilterHeader`, `useColumnExcelFilters` |
| Unified status | `ListStatusPill` |
| Multi-column sort | `useMultiSort` / shell sorts |
| **Infinite Loading** | `useInfiniteLoading`, `useListDataProvider`, `InfiniteSentinelRow` |
| Column management | `useColumnManager`, `ColumnManager` — **only via** `ListChrome` More (`⋮`) menu |
| User list preferences | `useListPreferences`, `listPreferencesService` |
| Selection count | `ListSelectionBar` — only after row selection; never permanent header totals |
| Composition | `ListColumnHeader`, `ListChrome` (More menu), `ListSelectionBar`, `useListShell` |

Pipeline: **Filter → Sort → Infinite Loading → List Rendering**.

Infinite Loading is the **only** large-list loading strategy. Do not expose pagination / virtual / mode toggles in UI or preferences.

---

## Module responsibility only

- Columns
- Rows / data source (client array or server-fed via `onLoadMore`)
- Business actions

Wired: Nabz, Kanoon, Vitrin, Gahshomar, Mowj.

---

## Rules

1. Do **not** build a new list outside this infrastructure.
2. Prefer `useListShell` + `ListChrome` for new module lists.
3. Column management and list-preference reset must **not** be always-visible header buttons — only via the More (`⋮`) menu on the left of the list header.
4. Do **not** show permanent record/result totals in the list header. Selection count belongs in `ListSelectionBar` and only when `selectedCount > 0`.
5. Persist only columns / order / widths / sorts / filters — never rendering strategy.
6. Do **not** add user-facing mode selection (`client` / `server` / `infinite` / `virtual` / pagination / virtual scroll).
7. Virtual windowing may be added **internally** later without changing module APIs.
8. Jarian CSS + theme tokens only — no Tailwind / Shadcn for list chrome.

## Not allowed

- Always-visible «ستون‌ها» / column-manager buttons in the list header
- Permanent «N رکورد» / total / result counters in the list header
- Module-local sort / infinite / filter / resize / status / column DnD
- Classic pagination footers on large CRM/ops lists
- User toggles for loading strategy
- Opportunistic third-party table kits
